<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bauchi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1809</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bauchi is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bauchi-state">Bauchi State</a>. It was founded around 1809 by Yakubu, a scholar and flag-bearer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>, as the capital of the Bauchi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. British forces occupied it in 1902, and it remains the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of Bauchi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bauchi.jpg" alt="Bauchi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BatureTaraba · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wikki_warm_spring_in_Yankari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
